WEBVTT

00:00.710 --> 00:05.940
Aoi sora miageru yoko-gao

00:05.940 --> 00:12.020
Tomatta toki no rasen

00:12.020 --> 00:18.590
ltsudemo ijippari de kimochi kakushite iru

00:18.590 --> 00:25.060
Setsunakute (koishikute)
Kurushiku naru

00:25.060 --> 00:28.830
Sonna ni tsuyokunai hazu

00:28.830 --> 00:36.240
Hontou wa futari no
kyori ni okubyou ni naru

00:36.240 --> 00:42.350
Sawatte hoshii no mai haato

00:42.350 --> 00:48.050
Toumawari shitemo tadoritsukeru no nara

00:48.050 --> 00:49.960
Sutaato rain

00:49.960 --> 00:54.530
Kokoro himotoku sutourii

00:54.530 --> 01:00.570
Namida ni sayonara shite
mirai o aruite yukou

01:00.570 --> 01:08.370
Mitsuketa yasashisa mune ni
daite yukeru kara

01:08.370 --> 01:15.210
Onegai ima dake wa sono mama de ite

01:27.660 --> 01:29.890
"Suzuka"

01:53.790 --> 01:55.650
Yo, good morning.

01:55.650 --> 01:57.320
Good morning.

01:57.320 --> 01:59.890
Your hair is sticking up.

01:59.890 --> 02:01.380
Huh?

02:04.860 --> 02:06.870
Always the same...

02:06.870 --> 02:10.930
What? It's just today.

02:14.510 --> 02:17.410
Hah! What's with her anyway?

02:19.540 --> 02:25.280
"Spring Storm"

02:28.620 --> 02:31.880
Keep scores for each other! No cheating!

02:38.960 --> 02:42.570
I'm going to do my best
for this P.E. Test...

02:42.570 --> 02:48.310
Huh? That's strange coming
from someone like you.

02:48.310 --> 02:51.380
I get excited about things like this.

02:51.380 --> 02:58.220
Besides, I was tops in P.E. At my
junior high school, except for one event.

02:58.220 --> 03:00.820
Really? Which one?

03:00.820 --> 03:02.910
Never mind.

03:04.090 --> 03:06.520
Let's start with the running broad jump.

03:06.520 --> 03:08.030
Not many people are over there...

03:08.030 --> 03:10.960
H-How about the vertical jump?

03:10.960 --> 03:13.030
There aren't many people
doing that, either.

03:13.030 --> 03:14.090
Huh?

03:16.000 --> 03:18.740
Owweee!

03:18.740 --> 03:21.570
Oh, I get it.

03:22.510 --> 03:25.480
Hey, don't get me wrong.

03:28.880 --> 03:34.750
Suzuka, you're paired up
with Sakurai. Can we join you?

03:34.750 --> 03:36.250
Fine with me.

03:36.250 --> 03:38.490
I'm okay, too.

03:38.490 --> 03:41.460
Did you hear that? Happy?

03:41.460 --> 03:44.260
Well, not really...

03:49.530 --> 03:53.800
Why don't you show us
your ace form from junior high?

03:53.800 --> 03:57.540
Ace form in junior high?

03:57.540 --> 04:00.940
Yeah, he was a star in his local school.

04:00.940 --> 04:02.450
Right?

04:02.450 --> 04:04.680
N-Not really...

04:07.520 --> 04:13.120
Go ahead and show us your skill.
You'll earn points with her.

04:17.330 --> 04:19.560
Okay, then...

04:20.600 --> 04:22.590
I'll keep record.

04:23.930 --> 04:27.570
Was he really number one in junior high?

04:27.570 --> 04:31.280
Yeah, that's what he told me...
except for one event.

04:31.280 --> 04:32.680
Which was?

04:32.680 --> 04:36.510
He didn't tell me.

04:36.510 --> 04:39.810
Let's see how he does.

04:45.590 --> 04:48.260
There!

04:48.260 --> 04:49.830
Wow!

04:49.830 --> 04:51.730
It's 72.5cm.

04:51.730 --> 04:52.700
That's great!

04:52.700 --> 04:56.200
Okay! That's a new record
for me! Did you see that?

04:56.200 --> 04:57.570
Am I awesome, or what?

05:00.040 --> 05:01.470
Huh?

05:01.470 --> 05:07.080
I expected you to be better because you
said you were number one in junior high.

05:07.080 --> 05:08.810
What?

05:19.590 --> 05:23.130
Wow! Suzuka, it's 84cm!

05:23.130 --> 05:26.230
E-Eighty four...

05:26.230 --> 05:29.360
No wonder she's a great high jumper.

05:30.830 --> 05:33.840
Eighty four centimeters...

05:33.840 --> 05:36.510
Okay! I did 84cm as well.

05:36.510 --> 05:39.140
Awesome, Hatori!

05:39.140 --> 05:41.580
Oh, you're pretty good.

05:54.360 --> 05:57.060
You're just awesome, Suzuka.

05:57.060 --> 06:00.830
So are you, Hatori. I'm impressed.

06:00.830 --> 06:03.200
You should do sports.

06:03.200 --> 06:06.900
No way, I'm not good enough.

06:06.900 --> 06:09.840
There're many people
better than me in this school.

06:09.840 --> 06:12.210
I think you're good enough...

06:13.480 --> 06:15.310
And compared to you...

06:16.510 --> 06:20.220
Come on, Yamato...

06:20.220 --> 06:25.560
I thought he could do better
because he came to a sports school.

06:25.560 --> 06:26.960
But he seems to be just average.

06:26.960 --> 06:32.000
He'd probably be tops at a regular school.

06:32.000 --> 06:35.400
Akitsuki, you'll do better
in another event...

06:35.400 --> 06:40.170
Nah. Next is the 50m run.

06:40.170 --> 06:42.110
There's no hope.

06:42.110 --> 06:44.870
Well, the one event he's not good at is...

06:46.480 --> 06:49.480
I used to be first all the time
at my elementary school.

06:49.480 --> 06:51.980
So I got cocky and entered
a city relay race

06:51.980 --> 06:56.350
in the summer of my
first year at junior high.

06:56.350 --> 07:02.430
My school didn't have a track & field club,
so I teamed up with three friends...

07:02.430 --> 07:04.930
How did you do?

07:04.930 --> 07:07.800
I was the anchor,

07:07.800 --> 07:10.430
but we ended up dead last
and everyone laughed at us.

07:10.430 --> 07:13.170
Since then, I haven't run short distances.

07:13.170 --> 07:16.770
I always made excuses
and tried to avoid it...

07:16.770 --> 07:18.140
Well...

07:19.480 --> 07:22.010
Boy, maybe I'll skip it.

07:22.010 --> 07:24.910
You can't do that. Come on.

07:33.160 --> 07:35.390
He looks miserable.

07:35.390 --> 07:39.760
Well, but he may do something unexpected
and surprise us yet.

07:39.760 --> 07:44.570
You think so? But his opponent
is Kobayakawa.

07:44.570 --> 07:48.210
Isn't he that scholarship student
who excels in short distances?

07:48.210 --> 07:50.240
It makes it even more interesting.

07:50.240 --> 07:52.710
Take your place at the starting line.

07:52.710 --> 07:54.200
Hmm...

08:01.950 --> 08:05.760
Oh? Does Yamato use an explosive start?

08:05.760 --> 08:10.630
I bet he thought he could run faster
if he kicked off with both legs.

08:10.630 --> 08:12.930
He's such an idiot.

08:12.930 --> 08:16.660
I could run faster if I kicked off
with both legs.

08:23.440 --> 08:26.340
Come on, Yamato!

08:30.380 --> 08:32.310
At this point...

08:35.020 --> 08:36.890
Ready!

08:36.890 --> 08:38.750
I can just give it my best.

08:44.760 --> 08:46.660
No way...

09:17.590 --> 09:19.660
Awesome! Great!

09:19.660 --> 09:21.700
5.93 seconds.

09:21.700 --> 09:24.740
Huh? Is that good?

09:24.740 --> 09:26.600
Hey, you're awesome!

09:26.600 --> 09:29.170
What did you do in junior high?

09:29.170 --> 09:30.170
Well...

09:30.170 --> 09:32.040
Did you already sign up?

09:32.040 --> 09:33.380
How about joining our track & field club?

09:33.380 --> 09:36.110
Oh, your speed might
be perfect for baseball.

09:36.110 --> 09:37.950
See, I told you.

09:37.950 --> 09:40.520
How did you know?

09:40.520 --> 09:44.220
Well, I knew he was
very quick in running away

09:44.220 --> 09:46.990
whenever we got into mischief.

09:46.990 --> 09:50.330
But what he said about that relay race
back in junior high...

09:50.330 --> 09:53.860
The other three must've been slow runners.

09:53.860 --> 09:56.900
He warmed the bench
in junior high baseball,

09:56.900 --> 09:59.200
but he can do well if he tries.

09:59.200 --> 10:03.510
Asahina! Everybody is impressed with me!

10:03.510 --> 10:07.080
Incredible! You're so fast, Akitsuki!

10:07.080 --> 10:09.510
Maybe...

10:09.510 --> 10:11.350
Right, Asahina?

10:11.350 --> 10:13.720
Yeah, I guess you're not bad.

10:13.720 --> 10:14.850
Huh?

10:14.850 --> 10:18.920
Let's go, Sakurai. It's our turn.

10:18.920 --> 10:20.580
Wait...

10:23.390 --> 10:26.800
Why is she like that? She's not impressed?

10:26.800 --> 10:31.940
Don't worry. You earned
some big points with her.

10:31.940 --> 10:35.340
I didn't run well for that reason.

10:43.550 --> 10:45.380
Asahina...

11:09.570 --> 11:11.670
What?

11:13.640 --> 11:16.410
Is there anything on my face?

11:16.410 --> 11:18.550
N-No...

11:18.550 --> 11:21.990
Yamato, I heard you beat the guy
with the scholarship

11:21.990 --> 11:24.150
in the short-distance run today.

11:24.150 --> 11:26.790
Awesome! I'm proud of you.

11:26.790 --> 11:28.460
Is that right?

11:28.460 --> 11:31.160
Yup. Hatori told me.

11:31.160 --> 11:35.700
Actually, I was the most surprised of all.

11:35.700 --> 11:38.670
And everyone was watching.

11:38.670 --> 11:42.240
Was he that fast?

11:42.240 --> 11:45.310
I guess he was average.

11:45.310 --> 11:50.010
- Hey, Asahina. Can't you at least-
- Thanks for dinner.

11:56.450 --> 11:58.150
What's wrong with her?

12:09.130 --> 12:11.770
Oh, Asahina, good morning.

12:11.770 --> 12:13.200
Good morning.

12:15.670 --> 12:18.230
Look, my hair is perfect today!

12:19.710 --> 12:21.680
I-I guess so...

12:27.820 --> 12:29.440
H-Hey...

12:32.960 --> 12:34.890
She looks strange...

12:35.160 --> 12:38.930
"Asahina Baths"

12:38.930 --> 12:41.430
"Asahina Baths"
Good morning, Suzuka.

12:41.430 --> 12:42.930
"Asahina Baths"
Good morning.

12:42.930 --> 12:45.140
"Asahina Baths"
I heard it'll be raining this afternoon.

12:45.140 --> 12:47.070
"Asahina Baths"
Take your umbrella with you.

12:47.070 --> 12:47.700
Take your umbrella with you.

12:47.700 --> 12:49.170
I have one...

12:51.110 --> 12:53.170
I'm off to school.

12:55.150 --> 12:58.080
Hey, Asahina.

12:58.080 --> 12:59.050
Yamato...

12:59.050 --> 13:00.780
Hey!

13:00.780 --> 13:02.120
Oh, well...

13:10.490 --> 13:12.930
You mean, Suzuka is acting strange?

13:12.930 --> 13:19.240
Yeah, she stares at me, then she's rude.

13:19.240 --> 13:21.940
I'm wondering if I did
something bad to her...

13:21.940 --> 13:26.610
Idiot. A girl acts like that
when she's in love.

13:26.610 --> 13:29.050
Huh? What do you mean?

13:29.050 --> 13:34.680
Y'know... don't you steal looks
at a girl you like?

13:34.680 --> 13:37.190
M-Maybe...

13:37.190 --> 13:39.660
You're shy toward girls,

13:39.660 --> 13:42.260
so you don't understand
what it is to be watched by a girl.

13:42.260 --> 13:43.530
Well...

13:43.530 --> 13:48.300
You earned big points
with her in P.E. Yesterday.

13:48.300 --> 13:51.730
Even I'm impressed that you ran so fast.

13:58.240 --> 14:02.640
But I don't think she'll like me
because of that.

14:04.110 --> 14:08.140
Love happens suddenly. Well, good luck.

14:12.520 --> 14:14.680
Suddenly, huh?

14:22.030 --> 14:26.970
Factor the cube of X and the cube of Y...

14:26.970 --> 14:30.410
Listen! This is important.

14:33.780 --> 14:36.300
She's in love.

14:44.350 --> 14:49.660
Really? Does Asahina like me?

14:52.730 --> 14:54.290
Hmm...

15:02.870 --> 15:06.380
Cripes, I can't go home like this.

15:06.380 --> 15:08.040
What should I do?

15:15.220 --> 15:17.990
Gee, I wish someone would
share an umbrella with me...

15:17.990 --> 15:20.190
Suzuka!

15:20.190 --> 15:22.190
Miki!

15:22.190 --> 15:26.430
We have rainy-day training
today in the weight room.

15:26.430 --> 15:29.230
Okay. Let's go to the gym then.

15:31.500 --> 15:35.340
Oh yeah... She has practice.

15:35.340 --> 15:36.570
Akitsuki.

15:36.570 --> 15:38.710
Huh?

15:38.710 --> 15:40.440
You don't have an umbrella, do you?

15:40.440 --> 15:43.680
We can share mine if you like...

15:43.680 --> 15:45.520
Uh... well...

15:45.520 --> 15:48.820
I'm afraid you'll get wet
and catch a cold again...

15:48.820 --> 15:52.490
Actually, I have a something to do...

15:52.490 --> 15:55.560
Really? I can wait...

15:55.560 --> 16:01.200
I mean, it's not important,
so I can do it tomorrow...

16:01.200 --> 16:03.930
Oh, I knew you'd
have an umbrella, Sakurai.

16:03.930 --> 16:05.270
Huh?

16:05.270 --> 16:12.940
Perfect timing! I'm about to go
to a party, but I forgot my umbrella.

16:12.940 --> 16:16.650
So, can you share your umbrella
with me all the way to the train station?

16:16.650 --> 16:19.350
I'll look dumb if I'm in wet clothes. Please!

16:19.350 --> 16:20.620
Uh... Well...

16:20.620 --> 16:23.590
Sorry Yamato, I'm going to
borrow your friend to go to the party.

16:23.590 --> 16:25.250
Huh?

16:45.540 --> 16:48.530
What am I doing here?

16:56.050 --> 17:01.120
Ah, how long does
weight training take anyway?

17:01.120 --> 17:03.220
Does she want more muscle?

17:05.030 --> 17:09.170
She looks perfect as she is now...

17:09.170 --> 17:12.400
Hey, what am I thinking about?

17:12.400 --> 17:14.670
Forget it! I'll just go home now!

17:14.670 --> 17:16.610
I'm not going to wait for her!

17:24.650 --> 17:29.950
Here's a more natural place to wait.
I guess I'll practice...

17:30.920 --> 17:34.490
Oh, Asahina, I forgot my umbrella.

17:34.490 --> 17:36.530
Can you share your umbrella with me?

17:36.530 --> 17:38.260
It's okay if you don't want to.

17:41.060 --> 17:43.170
Creepy, who is that?

17:43.170 --> 17:44.900
Maybe a stalker!

17:44.900 --> 17:46.340
Yuck!

17:46.340 --> 17:48.330
Oh, well... I should go home.

17:55.480 --> 17:59.150
Nah, maybe a little longer...

17:59.150 --> 18:01.280
Yamato.

18:01.280 --> 18:02.390
Oh?

18:02.390 --> 18:04.220
Ah, Asahina!

18:04.220 --> 18:06.920
I thought you already went home.

18:06.920 --> 18:10.860
You know, I'm having problems
opening my shoe box.

18:10.860 --> 18:12.230
It's open.

18:12.230 --> 18:15.660
Yeah, I just got it to open.

18:18.070 --> 18:20.440
You don't have your umbrella, do you?

18:20.440 --> 18:21.900
Do you want to share mine?

18:21.900 --> 18:26.140
Yeah, I forgot my umbrella!
Can you share yours?

18:26.140 --> 18:28.410
It's okay if you don't want to...

18:30.280 --> 18:32.050
R-Really?

18:32.050 --> 18:33.520
Yes.

19:23.370 --> 19:25.500
It's pretty windy.

19:25.500 --> 19:27.160
Yes.

19:31.740 --> 19:35.950
Is this what is called a spring storm?

19:35.950 --> 19:37.310
Maybe...

19:44.020 --> 19:48.830
She's more aloof now.

19:48.830 --> 19:51.890
I shouldn't believe what Yasunobu says.

19:54.630 --> 19:56.670
Yamato, you...

19:56.670 --> 19:58.630
Huh?

19:58.630 --> 20:01.340
...can run very fast.

20:01.340 --> 20:03.810
I guess so...

20:03.810 --> 20:09.750
You gained big points
with her in P.E. Yesterday.

20:09.750 --> 20:11.410
She can't be...

20:14.450 --> 20:17.440
Were you impressed, just a little bit?

20:18.890 --> 20:20.720
Uh-huh!

20:52.120 --> 20:54.250
A-Asahina?

21:04.200 --> 21:05.670
Oh!

21:40.500 --> 21:45.910
Kaze ni naru yo aoi fiirudo de

21:45.910 --> 21:48.710
lma wa tada...

21:48.710 --> 21:55.850
Choppiri "yake" ni
"atsuku" natte supiido agete

21:55.850 --> 21:56.520
lkou

21:56.520 --> 21:57.290
Hashiru

21:57.290 --> 21:57.890
Tomaru

21:57.890 --> 21:58.520
Susumu

21:58.520 --> 21:59.220
Hirumu

21:59.220 --> 21:59.890
Haneru

21:59.890 --> 22:01.860
Shagamu

22:01.860 --> 22:02.490
Utau

22:02.490 --> 22:03.160
Sakebu

22:03.160 --> 22:03.960
Michiru

22:03.960 --> 22:04.460
Kakeru

22:04.460 --> 22:06.630
lkiru koko de

22:06.630 --> 22:12.070
Konna mucha na ikikata mo manzara
waruku wa nai ne

22:12.070 --> 22:17.660
Nanika okiru sonna ki ga shiteru

22:19.410 --> 22:22.340
Aza-darake ni naru hibi ni

22:24.780 --> 22:32.420
"Genkai" o kanjiru hi mo arundakedo ne...

22:32.420 --> 22:37.490
Kaze ni naru yo aoi fiirudo de

22:37.490 --> 22:43.160
Isshun o hashiri-nukete iku

22:43.160 --> 22:48.300
Katachi nante kawatte iku mono dakara

22:48.300 --> 22:51.010
Tomerarenai...

22:51.010 --> 22:54.080
Choppiri "ganko" de "yancha"

22:54.080 --> 22:57.910
"Makezu-girai"

22:57.910 --> 22:58.580
Kokoro

22:58.580 --> 22:59.250
Hashiru

22:59.250 --> 22:59.910
Tomaru

22:59.910 --> 23:00.450
Susumu

23:00.450 --> 23:01.080
Hirumu

23:01.080 --> 23:01.720
Haneru

23:01.720 --> 23:03.950
Shagamu

23:03.950 --> 23:04.450
Utau

23:04.450 --> 23:05.120
Sakebu

23:05.120 --> 23:05.950
Michiru

23:05.950 --> 23:06.650
Kakeru

23:06.650 --> 23:09.820
lkiru koko de

23:10.330 --> 23:14.030
I really don't understand about
what goes on in a girl's mind.

23:14.030 --> 23:17.030
She suddenly gets upset or curt...

23:17.030 --> 23:19.470
What's on her mind, anyway?

23:19.470 --> 23:20.970
If you really want to know,
why don't you ask her?

23:20.970 --> 23:22.970
"Next episode: Lovesickness"
If you really want to know,
why don't you ask her?

23:22.970 --> 23:24.840
"Next episode: Lovesickness"
